WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:07.530
It's really important that I do this story
today before we get sucked into really unreasonable

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:10.830
and naive expectations about how the next
couple of years are going to go.

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:16.020
We need to reset our expectations for the
next couple of years, and this should help.

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:19.970
Some have been wondering, some have been asking
me, emailing me, David, what happens to these

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:22.940
anti Trump Republicans when Joe Biden wins?

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:24.470
What happens to the Lincoln Project?

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:25.610
What happens to the Kazik?

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:26.660
What happens to Romney?

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.510
Do they keep working with Democrats?

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:30.519
Do they support Biden's agenda?

00:00:30.519 --> 00:00:31.590
What happens?

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:34.660
And the answer is no to all of the above.

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:41.680
I have two quick clips to play for you today,
which will, in no time at all, disabuse you

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:45.560
of the notion that these anti Trump Republicans
are our friends.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:50.580
Now, to be very clear, if you take an anti
Trump Republican and you remove Trump, what

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:51.790
do you have left?

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:53.920
It's called the Republican, OK?

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.110
They become just Republicans.

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:58.400
When you remove Trump from the equation.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:00:59.649
Here is Mitt Romney.

00:00:59.649 --> 00:01:02.530
Strong, principled, anti Trump Republican.

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:03.530
Right.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:09.219
Telling Jake Tapper on CNN his priorities
now that Trump Reagan are blocking the green

00:01:09.219 --> 00:01:18.709
new deal, keeping gas, coal and oil and blocking
Medicare for all and blocking any tax increases.

00:01:18.709 --> 00:01:20.060
Take a look.

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:21.539
I'm not going to talk about my vote.

00:01:21.539 --> 00:01:22.729
That's in the rearview mirror.

00:01:22.729 --> 00:01:25.920
I'm going to talk now about how I can work
with the new president.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:30.299
I know he's on the other side of the aisle,
but I want to make sure that we conservatives

00:01:30.299 --> 00:01:33.719
keep on fighting to make sure that we don't
have a green new deal.

00:01:33.719 --> 00:01:40.009
We don't get rid of gas and coal and oil,
that we don't have a Medicare for all plan

00:01:40.009 --> 00:01:41.009
put in place.

00:01:41.009 --> 00:01:44.210
So we don't raise taxes on American enterprise
that would kill the economy.

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:49.679
So, look, I congratulate him, but I'm not
going to put aside conservative principles.

00:01:49.679 --> 00:01:51.649
We're going to fight for the things that we
believe in.

00:01:51.649 --> 00:01:54.270
So he was against Trump.

00:01:54.270 --> 00:02:00.849
Principled voted even to convict Trump on
impeachment on one of the two counts, and

00:02:00.849 --> 00:02:05.859
his policies are still awful and now his priority
is blocking the things that Joe Biden says

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:07.380
he's going to do.

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:15.040
Mitt Romney, now that Joe Biden will be president,
immediately returns to making his focus, preventing

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:19.049
us from putting policies in place that would
be good for the environment and good for people

00:02:19.049 --> 00:02:20.790
and good for the economy.

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:22.050
These are not our friends.

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:26.700
And I was wrong because I previously said
the day Biden is inaugurated, they go back

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.340
to being their nonsensical selves.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:33.930
I underestimated the day after Biden was called
the winner, they went back to being their

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:35.159
nonsensical selves.

00:02:35.159 --> 00:02:36.840
Here's another one.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:41.660
Reasonable anti Trump Republican John Kasich
supported Biden.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:44.170
He goes on CNN and says, Joe Biden one.

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:45.170
Great.

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:50.530
Now Biden needs to do what Republicans want
and make sure that the left of the Democratic

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:52.810
Party isn't listened to.

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:57.109
And Kasich even goes on to say that the far
left almost cost Biden the election.

00:02:57.109 --> 00:03:00.650
And right on cue, I have joked that they would
do this.

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:05.370
John Kasich actually brings up you know, we've
got big debt problems to solve.

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:06.650
It is beyond parody.

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:10.400
I told you, you're ready for them to talk
about the debt again.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:11.400
Right.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.840
And and right on cue, John Kasich is doing
it.

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:17.129
Now is the time for Democrats.

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:22.330
And I believe Joe Biden will do this to begin
to listen to what the other half the country

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:23.330
has had to say.

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:29.010
But we have to listen to what those folks,
those Republicans all across this country

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:30.840
has had to say.

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:35.489
The best thing that's happened to Joe Biden
is the fact that the United States Senate

00:03:35.489 --> 00:03:40.310
is either going to be Republican or very close
and the far left can push him as hard as they

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:41.310
want.

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:44.819
And frankly, the Democrats have to make it
clear to the far left that they almost cost

00:03:44.819 --> 00:03:45.880
him this election.

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:50.799
And that congresswoman from Virginia warned
the Democrats, you want to talk about defunding

00:03:50.799 --> 00:03:52.920
the police, you'll have no support.

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:57.599
And I think this is an opportunity for Biden
to talk about, you know, the center right

00:03:57.599 --> 00:04:01.640
and the center left of this country and what
can be achieved because we have enormous problems

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:07.790
with debt, Social Security, Medicare, health
care, little steps, little steps.

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:13.329
One other thing, one Democrat told me at some
point, if they have been more clear in rejecting

00:04:13.329 --> 00:04:18.880
the hard left, they would have appealed more
to Americans who I believe essentially live

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:19.880
in the middle.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:25.160
So I think actually he's in a better position
today because being pulled from the left isn't

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:26.160
going to work.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:30.130
So they are doing every single thing that
Republicans always do.

00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:31.759
They've learned nothing.

00:04:31.759 --> 00:04:36.650
They've changed nothing from this Trump experience
during Trump.

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:38.530
Some of them oppose Trump.

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:39.530
Biden wins now.

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:43.140
It's resist the influence from the hard left.

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:45.039
We've got to deal with the debt.

00:04:45.039 --> 00:04:49.580
We've got to find common ground, which, by
the way, when they win, they never have to

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:53.650
find common ground, common ground they want
when they lose.

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:57.470
Democrats have catered to the middle, like
Kasich says, for decades.

00:04:57.470 --> 00:05:04.449
And now Biden won thanks to the activism of
the left in places like Georgia and others.

00:05:04.449 --> 00:05:09.360
So the last thing Joe Biden should be doing
is listening to the people.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:13.310
First of all, he shouldn't be listening to
Kasich or Romney, and he certainly shouldn't

00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:18.110
be listening to the people Kasich and Romney
want Biden to listen to.

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:23.840
It's I have like whiplash from how quickly
these Republicans go right back to their tired

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:24.840
old lines.

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:25.889
I told you it would happen.

00:05:25.889 --> 00:05:26.409
And it has.

